# Learnings

When Courtney says `learn!` after a correction:

1. Identify the problem created and why it was a problem.
2. Identify how she said to fix it.
3. Write a 1-to-4-sentence learning. Put it in the Learnings section of the most relevant `.cursor/rules/` file, or as `docs/agents/learnings/YYYY-MM-DD-<slug>.md` when the lesson is non-obvious, verified, and durable.

Each learning has a counter. Increase it when a learning was useful. Decrease it when it caused more problems. Remove a learning whose counter hits zero and that keeps causing harm.

Do not invent learnings. Wait for a correction or a verified durable lesson.

